# Bill of Materials (BOM)
 
**Version:** 1.0

## Complete Parts List

| 1  | Arduino Nano             | 1  |
| 2  | HC-05 Bluetooth Module   | 1  |
| 3  | L298N Motor Driver       | 1  |
| 4  | DC Motors (with Gearbox) | 2  | 
| 5  | Custom tracked chassis   | 1  |
| 6  | Battery  3.7V            | 1  |
| 7  | 5V Boost Regulator       | 1  |
| 8  | Power Switch             | 1  |
| 9  | Jumper Wires             | 20 | 
| 10 | USB Programming Cable    | 1  |
| 11 | LED                      | 2  | 
| 12 | battery charge module    | 2  |
| 13 | 5V Relay module          | 2  | 
---

> **Minimum Battery Capacity:** 2000mAh for 1 hour operation

The l298n motor drive input voltage is between 5 and 28 so you can use the 7th part
with 1 battery or without that and connect to batteries for having the 7.4V. 
but in the second way you will need a 2 cell battery charger or take out the batteries and charge them one after one . 
